@0    = ~This is getting quite simply embarrassing. Do you really think you're going to get <CHARNAME>'s attention with card tricks and, and grinning like that all the time?~
@1    = ~Hey, he can give his attention to whatever he wants. You don't see me stopping you from talking about your charity missions, now do you?~
@2    = ~What exactly is THAT supposed to mean?~
@3    = ~Oh, come on, Nalia. You know, if you showed him a good time maybe he'd pay you a bit more attention.~
@4    = ~How dare you! You're so - you're such a - you're a vulgar little man, and I won't listen to any more of this!~
@5    = ~Oh, for pity's sake, please stop yawning!~
@6    = ~No need to snip at me just 'cause some of us have more interesting evenings than you, Lady de'Arnise.~
@7    = ~Oh, and what exactly do your evenings entail? As if I couldn't guess!~
@8    = ~I could tell you, but it'd make your hair curl.~
@9    = ~Right, that's it! I'm sick of you parading around with <CHARNAME> like some sort of - of--~
@10   = ~'Person having fun'?~
@11   = ~Yes. No!~
@12   = ~<CHARNAME>, please. I need to know, before I make a complete fool of myself. Do you have...feelings for Faren?~
@13   = ~Nalia, you know I only have eyes for you.~
@14   = ~Faren's just a bit of fun. I do like you a great deal, Nalia.~
@15   = ~I'm afraid I do prefer Faren's company to yours.~
@16   = ~All you talk about is politics. I'm not interested, Nalia.~
@17   = ~That's nice. That's really nice. Whatever, <CHARNAME>. Watch out for those mixed signals in future.~
@18   = ~My, he's looking put-out. Never mind, <CHARNAME>. I'm sure he'll be fine.~
@19   = ~Well, if you're not interested then I shan't bother you with my thoughts!~
@20   = ~Looks like Miss Priss's hair's in a knot. Oh, well - come here, <CHARNAME>, and we can talk as we walk.~
